{title: Nothing but the Blood of Jesus}
{artist: Robert Lowry (1826-1899)}
{key: G}
{copyright: Public Domain}

{sov: Verse 1}
What can [G]wash away my sin?
Nothing but the [D]blood of [G]Jesus;
What can [G]make me whole again?
Nothing but the [D]blood of [G]Jesus.
{eov}

{soc}
O [G]precious is the flow
That [D]makes me white as snow;
No [G]other fount I know,
Nothing but the [D]blood of [G]Jesus.
{eoc}

{sov: Verse 2}
For my [G]pardon, this I see,
Nothing but the [D]blood of [G]Jesus;
For my [G]cleansing this my plea,
Nothing but the [D]blood of [G]Jesus.
{eov}

{soc}
O [G]precious is the flow
That [D]makes me white as snow;
No [G]other fount I know,
Nothing but the [D]blood of [G]Jesus.
{eoc}

{sov: Verse 3}
Nothing [G]can for sin atone,
Nothing but the [D]blood of [G]Jesus;
Naught of [G]good that I have done,
Nothing but the [D]blood of [G]Jesus.
{eov}

{soc}
O [G]precious is the flow
That [D]makes me white as snow;
No [G]other fount I know,
Nothing but the [D]blood of [G]Jesus.
{eoc}

{sov: Verse 4}
This is [G]all my hope and peace,
Nothing but the [D]blood of [G]Jesus;
This is [G]all my righteousness,
Nothing but the [D]blood of [G]Jesus.
{eov}

{soc}
O [G]precious is the flow
That [D]makes me white as snow;
No [G]other fount I know,
Nothing but the [D]blood of [G]Jesus.
{eoc}
